00:33:52.895 --> 00:33:55.094
the time with my wife and my kids

00:33:55.094 --> 00:33:56.855
makes me a better dad it really does.

00:33:56.855 --> 00:33:57.904
It makes me a better husband,

00:33:57.904 --> 00:33:58.961
and I'm not guilty, also,

00:33:58.961 --> 00:34:00.656
because I know she's got a day, too.

00:34:00.656 --> 00:34:02.189
Our fourth bullet point is that

00:34:02.189 --> 00:34:04.579
every weekend, two days,

00:34:04.579 --> 00:34:06.429
we have one day

00:34:06.429 --> 00:34:08.626
of the two that's just our family

00:34:08.626 --> 00:34:10.190
just to kind of, you know,

00:34:10.190 --> 00:34:11.514
incubate, have that family time,

00:34:11.514 --> 00:34:13.203
and those four bullet points

00:34:13.203 --> 00:34:14.817
like the time I'm going to be away

00:34:14.817 --> 00:34:16.101
are nights out,

00:34:16.101 --> 00:34:17.357
and the time together on weekends

00:34:17.357 --> 00:34:18.508
helps me have a bit of

00:34:18.508 --> 00:34:21.663
a personal contract that if I break it,

00:34:21.663 --> 00:34:22.716
someone that travels a lot,

00:34:22.716 --> 00:34:23.777
then I know the next weekend,

00:34:23.777 --> 00:34:24.610
or the next week

00:34:24.610 --> 00:34:25.650
I got to make it up again.

00:34:25.650 --> 00:34:26.789
I think having a personal contract

00:34:26.789 --> 00:34:27.877
is just as important

00:34:27.877 --> 00:34:29.236
as having an employment contract.

00:34:29.236 --> 00:34:30.588
- Is this covered in your book?

00:34:30.588 --> 00:34:32.019
- It's not, it's bonus just for

00:34:32.019 --> 00:34:33.524
Evan Carmichael's YouTube channel.

00:34:33.524 --> 00:34:34.952
It's something that you know what?

00:34:34.952 --> 00:34:36.447
I've been talking a lot about recently,

00:34:36.447 --> 00:34:38.117
and I'm getting a reaction to it,

00:34:38.117 --> 00:34:39.404
and I'm thinking it's something

00:34:39.404 --> 00:34:40.852
I need to write something new about

00:34:40.852 --> 00:34:42.041
on this topic because it's something

00:34:42.041 --> 00:34:43.108
I've been doing for years.

00:34:43.108 --> 00:34:44.614
I had a boss when I worked at

00:34:44.614 --> 00:34:46.071
Walmart for a decade who said

00:34:46.071 --> 00:34:47.352
every time you take a new job

00:34:47.352 --> 00:34:49.186
we give you a work contract.

00:34:49.186 --> 00:34:51.701
You travel more, you make more money,

00:34:51.701 --> 00:34:52.946
you work more hours,

00:34:52.946 --> 00:34:54.105
but you don't go home and say,

00:34:54.105 --> 00:34:55.519
hey, what does this mean for

00:34:55.519 --> 00:34:57.083
number of dinners at home?

00:34:57.083 --> 00:34:57.921
What does this mean for

00:34:57.921 --> 00:34:58.754
number of weekends away?

00:34:58.754 --> 00:35:01.138
Write those things that are home, too,

00:35:01.138 --> 00:35:02.533
so that you don't apply

00:35:02.533 --> 00:35:04.742
stress and pressure on one system

00:35:04.742 --> 00:35:06.468
in exchange for the other.

00:35:06.468 --> 00:35:07.677
Because I started doing that for work

00:35:07.677 --> 00:35:09.037
then as I became an entrepreneur,

00:35:09.037 --> 00:35:09.915
as I'm starting to write,

00:35:09.915 --> 00:35:11.013
and speak full-time

00:35:11.013 --> 00:35:12.613
it became natural for me

00:35:12.613 --> 00:35:13.959
to write this document out

00:35:13.959 --> 00:35:15.206
in my personal life, too.

00:35:15.206 --> 00:35:17.436
- How do you decide how much of it

00:35:17.436 --> 00:35:18.769
you do yourself

00:35:19.921 --> 00:35:21.483
because some of them are personal,

00:35:21.483 --> 00:35:23.123
and then how much you're bringing

00:35:23.123 --> 00:35:26.172
to do as a joy exercise with your wife?

00:35:26.172 --> 00:35:27.219
- The way I think about it is

00:35:27.219 --> 00:35:28.475
yes, I'm an entrepreneur.

00:35:28.475 --> 00:35:30.572
I am writing, I am speaking.

00:35:30.572 --> 00:35:31.895
I'm trying to share these messages

00:35:31.895 --> 00:35:33.185
about positivity around the world.

00:35:33.185 --> 00:35:35.265
I believe that I am working

00:35:35.265 --> 00:35:36.905
to increase happiness in organizations,

00:35:36.905 --> 00:35:37.970
and what I'm passionate about,

00:35:37.970 --> 00:35:40.862
but I am living inside a system that

00:35:40.862 --> 00:35:42.915
I love with my wife, with my children

00:35:42.915 --> 00:35:45.697
that is as or more important to me,

00:35:45.697 --> 00:35:47.674
and that system has to be healthy,

00:35:47.674 --> 00:35:49.014
it has to be functional.

00:35:49.014 --> 00:35:50.217
It has to have great food,

00:35:50.217 --> 00:35:51.886
great dinners, great love,

00:35:51.886 --> 00:35:52.831
great vacations.

00:35:52.831 --> 00:35:54.821
If I'm being irresponsible to that

00:35:54.821 --> 00:35:57.343
system what's the point?

00:35:57.343 --> 00:35:59.019
It's all through conversation.

00:35:59.019 --> 00:36:00.174
It's all through organic.

00:36:00.174 --> 00:36:01.428
You write out what works for you

00:36:01.428 --> 00:36:03.513
I shared the travel, the time together,

00:36:03.513 --> 00:36:04.882
the nights out for energy

00:36:04.882 --> 00:36:06.028
because that's what works for us.

00:36:06.028 --> 00:36:07.259
You could have your own things.

00:36:07.259 --> 00:36:08.228
It could be about exercise.

00:36:08.228 --> 00:36:10.096
It could be about personal vacation.

00:36:10.096 --> 00:36:11.593
It could be about, you know,

00:36:11.593 --> 00:36:12.604
whatever works for you.

00:36:12.604 --> 00:36:13.437
I just think that

00:36:13.437 --> 00:36:14.460
having that personal contract

00:36:14.460 --> 00:36:15.293
is something that we don't have

00:36:15.293 --> 00:36:16.180
enough as entrepreneurs

00:36:16.180 --> 00:36:17.448
in the back of our minds

00:36:17.448 --> 00:36:20.068
as we're living these busy hectic lives.

00:36:20.068 --> 00:36:21.167
We're constantly trading off

00:36:21.167 --> 00:36:23.655
our personal for work

00:36:23.655 --> 00:36:25.675
when there should be two contracts.

00:36:25.675 --> 00:36:26.942
- How often are you

00:36:26.942 --> 00:36:28.377
revisiting those contracts?

00:36:28.377 --> 00:36:29.547
- About once a year,

00:36:29.547 --> 00:36:30.708
about once a year

00:36:30.708 --> 00:36:32.294
because it exists on paper,

00:36:32.294 --> 00:36:33.195
and you actually write it out,

00:36:33.195 --> 00:36:34.296
and you sign it.

00:36:34.296 --> 00:36:36.180
- Wow, it's a serious contract.

00:36:36.180 --> 00:36:37.013
- Oh, it's a real contract.

00:36:37.013 --> 00:36:37.846
- Okay.

00:36:37.846 --> 00:36:39.756
- That's why it comes to life is

00:36:39.756 --> 00:36:41.422
because you're putting ink on paper here.

00:36:41.422 --> 00:36:42.874
Not quite blood on paper,

00:36:42.874 --> 00:36:44.113
but it's like pretty serious,

00:36:44.113 --> 00:36:46.000
but if you break it, if you break it

00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:47.357
if I don't have an NNO,

00:36:47.357 --> 00:36:48.704
and I'm kind of frustrated

00:36:48.704 --> 00:36:49.699
I need two the next week

00:36:49.699 --> 00:36:50.532
to make up for it.

00:36:50.532 --> 00:36:51.365
If we don't have

00:36:51.365 --> 00:36:52.198
a day together on the weekend

00:36:52.198 --> 00:36:53.031
because there's a birthday party,

00:36:53.031 --> 00:36:54.014
and we're seeing our parents,

00:36:54.014 --> 00:36:55.440
and you know I'm traveling

00:36:55.440 --> 00:36:56.273
for one of the days,

00:36:56.273 --> 00:36:57.106
or we have stuff going on

00:36:57.106 --> 00:36:58.649
we know we need the full weekend

00:36:58.649 --> 00:37:00.271
next week to kind of incubate,

00:37:00.271 --> 00:37:02.534
so it creates pressure

00:37:02.534 --> 00:37:04.630
on you in a way that I think

00:37:04.630 --> 00:37:05.922
is ultimately healthy.

00:37:05.922 --> 00:37:06.755
- I loved it,

00:37:06.755 --> 00:37:07.588
well, thank you for sharing.

00:37:07.588 --> 00:37:09.755
- Thank you for having me.

00:37:10.748 --> 00:37:11.581
- So thank you guys

00:37:11.581 --> 00:37:13.827
so much for watching.

00:37:13.827 --> 00:37:15.590
- We made this video for Jason Fonseca.

00:37:15.590 --> 00:37:16.536
Jason, thank you so much.

00:37:16.536 --> 00:37:17.772
I hope we get to meet in person one day.

00:37:17.772 --> 00:37:19.324
- I'd love to know which one of

00:37:19.324 --> 00:37:21.694
Neil's rules you like the most,

00:37:21.694 --> 00:37:23.572
and what was the biggest takeaway lesson

00:37:23.572 --> 00:37:24.860
that you learned from him

00:37:24.860 --> 00:37:25.822
in this video?

00:37:25.822 --> 00:37:27.747
Please leave it in the comments below,

00:37:27.747 --> 00:37:29.622
and we're going to join in the discussion.

00:37:29.622 --> 00:37:31.113
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:37:31.113 --> 00:37:32.650
Continue to believe,

00:37:32.650 --> 00:37:34.567
and we'll see you soon.

00:37:40.949 --> 00:37:43.814
- Is this a good use of your time?

00:37:43.814 --> 00:37:46.064
(applause)

00:37:48.015 --> 00:37:50.682
What is a good use of your time?

00:37:59.934 --> 00:38:01.547
Could a conversation that

00:38:01.547 --> 00:38:03.786
was just questions be

00:38:03.786 --> 00:38:05.786
a good use of your time?

00:38:11.812 --> 00:38:13.593
What if the only time

00:38:13.593 --> 00:38:15.204
everyone is thinking

00:38:15.204 --> 00:38:17.371
is when no one is talking?

00:38:49.955 --> 00:38:52.372
What if instead of a TED Talk

00:38:53.427 --> 00:38:56.344
we did the first ever TED Listened?

00:39:01.508 --> 00:39:02.743
Do we give ourselves enough time

00:39:02.743 --> 00:39:05.993
to just stop, ask questions, and think?

00:39:15.017 --> 00:39:17.767
What do your best days look like?

00:39:30.455 --> 00:39:32.705
Is time you enjoyed wasting

00:39:33.616 --> 00:39:35.199
really wasted time?

00:39:49.336 --> 00:39:50.190
Do you remember when

00:39:50.190 --> 00:39:52.273
summer felt like forever?

00:39:56.886 --> 00:39:58.557
How do we live so that

00:39:58.557 --> 00:40:00.974
it always feels like forever?

00:40:13.288 --> 00:40:15.955
Why do more of us live alone now

00:40:17.230 --> 00:40:19.405
compared to any other time

00:40:19.405 --> 00:40:21.322
in our species history?

00:40:34.028 --> 00:40:37.439
Why have suicide rates globally

00:40:37.439 --> 00:40:39.856
recently passed murder rates?

00:40:47.414 --> 00:40:48.247
Could it be that

00:40:48.247 --> 00:40:50.204
the most dangerous person to you

00:40:50.204 --> 00:40:52.287
in the whole world is now

00:40:53.237 --> 00:40:54.070
you?

00:41:04.168 --> 00:41:05.814
Why do we fight more

00:41:05.814 --> 00:41:07.897
with people we love most?

00:41:22.015 --> 00:41:23.938
If you live with a partner

00:41:23.938 --> 00:41:25.574
does your partner meet all your

00:41:25.574 --> 00:41:27.876
social, intellectual,

00:41:27.876 --> 00:41:29.459
and physical needs?

00:41:36.955 --> 00:41:38.372
What do you need?

00:41:47.523 --> 00:41:50.887
How do we stop living in the past,

00:41:50.887 --> 00:41:52.387
and in the future?

00:41:55.466 --> 00:41:58.247
How do we make right now,

00:41:58.247 --> 00:42:00.080
right now feel longer?

00:42:06.953 --> 00:42:08.975
Does right now actually exist,

00:42:08.975 --> 00:42:11.172
or is it just where the past,

00:42:11.172 --> 00:42:13.839
and the future touch each other?

00:42:18.063 --> 00:42:20.328
Like why does the year 2000

00:42:20.328 --> 00:42:22.911
feel closer than the year 2032?

00:42:45.113 --> 00:42:48.196
Do we get to choose what we remember?

00:43:00.330 --> 00:43:03.080
How do you want to be remembered?

00:43:05.803 --> 00:43:08.053
How will you be remembered?

00:43:12.570 --> 00:43:14.834
Or would you choose to

00:43:14.834 --> 00:43:17.001
live forever if you could?

00:43:26.327 --> 00:43:27.244
Or is death

00:43:28.564 --> 00:43:31.522
like that tinfoil backing that

00:43:31.522 --> 00:43:33.130
a mirror needs

00:43:33.130 --> 00:43:35.713
if we are able to see anything?

00:43:50.736 --> 00:43:52.103
How well do you know

00:43:52.103 --> 00:43:54.770
your grandparent's grandparents?

00:44:03.979 --> 00:44:05.720
How well will your

00:44:05.720 --> 00:44:08.577
grandchildren's grandchildren

00:44:08.577 --> 00:44:10.327
know or remember you?

00:44:18.050 --> 00:44:19.726
Is there something you feel

00:44:19.726 --> 00:44:21.809
like you just have to do?

00:44:33.285 --> 00:44:34.554
Should you drop everything

00:44:34.554 --> 00:44:36.265
you're doing except

00:44:36.265 --> 00:44:39.432
the biggest possible thing you can do?

00:44:47.597 --> 00:44:49.196
Who invented your shoes?

00:44:49.196 --> 00:44:50.660
Who invented your glasses,

00:44:50.660 --> 00:44:54.288
your books, your foods, your religion?

00:44:54.288 --> 00:44:55.721
Who discovered your city,

00:44:55.721 --> 00:44:57.845
your country, your company?

00:44:57.845 --> 00:44:59.678
Do we know their name?

00:45:02.679 --> 00:45:05.762
Do we know how much they've given us?

00:45:17.683 --> 00:45:18.516
What story

00:45:20.620 --> 00:45:21.453
idea,

00:45:23.180 --> 00:45:24.597
or child of yours

00:45:26.018 --> 00:45:27.961
might survive

00:45:27.961 --> 00:45:30.211
as a tiny, flickering light

00:45:31.228 --> 00:45:34.653
deep in the pitch black darkness of

00:45:34.653 --> 00:45:37.049
the millions and million year future

00:45:37.049 --> 00:45:39.216
we can't possibly imagine?

00:45:46.876 --> 00:45:49.876
What if we're all just baton passers

00:45:51.314 --> 00:45:53.397
desperately, frantically,

00:45:54.648 --> 00:45:56.798
urgently trying to take

00:45:56.798 --> 00:46:00.384
the best of everything we've been given

00:46:00.384 --> 00:46:02.058
to give the future

00:46:02.058 --> 00:46:04.058
the best of what we got?

00:46:14.344 --> 00:46:16.427
Who are you in this with?

00:46:19.056 --> 00:46:21.639
How will you measure your life?

00:46:29.639 --> 00:46:31.222
What is your baton?

00:46:36.672 --> 00:46:39.902
How will you maximize your tiny

00:46:39.902 --> 00:46:40.819
short life?

00:46:45.986 --> 00:46:46.986
How will you

00:46:48.095 --> 00:46:48.928
maximize

00:46:50.222 --> 00:46:51.806
your tiny

00:46:51.806 --> 00:46:52.981
short

00:46:52.981 --> 00:46:53.814
life?

00:47:25.631 --> 00:47:27.178
Any questions?

00:47:27.178 --> 00:47:30.345
(cheers and applause)

